    "probe_text": "I've read the endpoint YAML and every function class in the pipeline. Here is the complete, ordered account of what `POST /api/owners` does.\n\n## Gate (whole endpoint)\n\n- **0. Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. The caller must hold `OWNER_ADMIN` or the request is denied before any step runs. Everything below runs inside a single `transaction` governance that commits once at the end.\n\n## The pipeline (in execution order)\n\n**1. CheckIdempotencyKey** *(side-effect + branch)*\nReads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header and publishes it. If the key was previously used **and** the owner it created still exists, it republishes that owner and takes the **replay** branch \u2192 `RespondWithOwner` returns the existing owner with **200**, skipping the entire create pipeline. Otherwise it proceeds.\n\n**2. ValidateNewOwner** *(validation)* \u2014 reads the request body (the one and only body read). Rejects with `MissingOwnerFieldsException` if any required field is missing/blank: `firstName`, `lastName`, address (either a non-blank structured `addressLine1` **or** a non-blank flat `address`), `city`, `telephone`.\n\n**3. ValidateRegistrationDate** *(validation)* \u2014 `registrationDate` is optional; if supplied and later than the server's current date \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n\n**4. ValidateOwnerPostcode** *(validation)* \u2014 `postcode` optional; if present it must be a 4-digit value valid for the city's region \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n\n**5. NormalizeOwnerAddress** *(side-effect)* \u2014 normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` in place and sets the flat `address` to its canonical form, mutating the shared request.\n\n**6. NormalizeOwnerTelephone** *(validation + side-effect)* \u2014 converts `telephone` to E.164 and stores it back; if it can't form valid E.164 or the national-number length is wrong for the country code \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n\n**7. NormalizeOwnerEmail** *(validation + side-effect)* \u2014 `email` optional; if present it must match the email syntax pattern \u2192 else `InvalidEmailException` (400); a valid address is trimmed and lower-cased back onto the request.\n\n**8. ValidateEmailDomain** *(validation)* \u2014 if an email is present and its domain is on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400).\n\n**9. EnsureUniqueIdentity** *(validation)* \u2014 computes the derived identity key and compares against all non-deleted owners (recomputed); an exact whole-key match \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409). Soft-deleted owners don't block.\n\n**10. EnsureUniqueHousehold** *(validation)* \u2014 skipped if the request declares `sharesHousehold` or has no postcode; otherwise if an existing non-deleted owner shares the household id (lastName + postcode) \u2192 `HouseholdDuplicateException` (409).\n\n**11. EnsureCityHasCapacity** *(validation)* \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, trimmed); if \u2265 **50** \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n**12. EnsureDailyLimit** *(validation)* \u2014 counts owners already registered on the request's effective business day; if \u2265 **100** \u2192 `DailyLimitExceededException` (429).\n\n**13. BuildOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 maps the validated/normalized DTO to a new `Owner` entity.\n\n**14. ResolveRegistrationDate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets the effective registration date on the entity: supplied date or today, then rolled forward to a business day (a weekend becomes the following Monday).\n\n**15. AssignCustomerCode** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode; hash over normalized telephone + last name), de-duplicated with a `-<n>` suffix against existing codes.\n\n**16. AssignHouseholdId** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `householdId` from last name + postcode.\n\n**17. AssignIdentityKey** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `identityKey` (from normalized telephone, email, household id) so the stored/returned key matches the one used for duplicate detection.\n\n**18. CountNamesakes** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive), counted before this save.\n\n**19. CountHouseholdMembers** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `householdSize` = 1 + existing owners sharing the household id.\n\n**20. FlagBulkSignup** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning` true if more than **80** owners are already registered on the effective day (soft warning below the hard daily cap).\n\n**21. FlagPossibleDuplicate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`; forced false when `sharesHousehold` is declared or there's no postcode, otherwise true if an existing owner shares the household id.\n\n**22. SaveOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 persists the owner via the repository.\n\n**23. RecordIdempotencyKey** *(side-effect)* \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, records key \u2192 new owner id so a future identical request replays instead of duplicating.\n\n**24. AuditOwnerCreated** *(side-effect)* \u2014 logs an audit line on the `AUDIT` logger (owner id, customer code, registration date, membership points/level/number).\n\n**25. RespondWithOwnerCreated** *(response)* \u2014 sends **201 Created** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header and the `OwnerDto` body.\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Validation ordering is deliberate:** required-fields \u2192 date \u2192 postcode \u2192 normalization \u2192 email domain \u2192 uniqueness/capacity/rate guards. Normalization (steps 5\u20137) runs *before* the uniqueness checks (9\u201310) and the derived-key/code assignments so those all operate on canonical values.\n- The soft-deleted skip in the uniqueness checks and the \"count before save\" behavior of the flagging steps mean these reflect state *prior* to this insert.\n- Anything thrown maps to a status via the handlers in `officefloor/escalation/` (the parenthesized codes above); unmatched exceptions fall through to Spring's advice."
